Everywhere: Keep desktop-Linux-only code paths off Android

Bionic defines __linux__, so AK_OS_LINUX is set on Android, but CMake's LINUX
is not, so the Linux-only sources (Seccomp.cpp, the Compositor/MediaServer
SandboxLinux.cpp, SystemFFmpeg*.cpp, CrashReportPOSIX.cpp) are not built for
Android while code guarded by AK_OS_LINUX still calls into them. Linking
Compositor, MediaServer and the Android UI library failed with undefined
symbols. Exclude Android at those call sites; Android uses the unimplemented
sandbox and crash report stubs until it gets a sandbox of its own.

Requirement: SEC-020

